# Personal data — never commit (contains contact info, work history, Q&A answers)
# NOTE: must be profile/* (not profile/) — git never descends into a fully
# ignored directory, which would make the example-file negation dead.
profile/*
!profile/profile.example.yaml
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and it must stay that way. An unanchored
# `jobs/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently
# swallowed all 8 of Phase 3's input fixtures in
# tests/documents/assemble/jobs/ — their golden files committed, their inputs
# did not, so the byte-identical check would have been untestable on a fresh
# clone while passing locally. Found by qa (QA-B1-5) via the
# "nothing under tests/ is gitignored" test, which exists for exactly this.
# The personal data this protects is the per-job workspace tree, and that
# lives only at the repo root.
/jobs/

# Scratch copies of the fact base. docs/next-session-prompt.md documents a
# repair recipe that stages the real answers.yaml at the REPO ROOT:
#   head -n 234 profile/answers.yaml > answers.tmp && mv answers.tmp profile/...
# `profile/*` does not cover the root, so a half-run recipe leaves the user's
# answers sitting outside every ignore rule. Found untracked and uncovered on
# 2026-07-31 (0 bytes that time). tests/hooks/repo-hygiene.test.mjs asserts it.
*.tmp

# Secrets — never commit; use .env.example as the template
.env

# Dependencies / build
node_modules/
*.log

# Playwright MCP browser artifacts (snapshots/console logs from apply sessions)
# BOTH of these hold the user's REAL ATS session cookies. That is the whole
# reason they are here, and it is why neither may ever be committed.
#   .playwright-mcp/  is MCP-owned and the only place a login ever happens
#   .playwright-auto/ is the unattended runner's, refreshed by auth-sync.mjs
# .playwright-auto/ was missing until 2026-07-31 and auth-sync.mjs refuses to
# run without it (code: "not_ignored") — a deliberate refusal rather than a
# silent sync into a tracked directory. Found by w4-autonomy while building
# that script; added by build-manager rather than ci-engineer, whose file this
# is, because an un-ignored cookie store is a live credential-leak risk and
# adding an ignore line only ever narrows what can be committed.
.playwright-mcp/
.playwright-auto/

# Rendered artifacts outside jobs/
*.pdf
*.html
!templates/*.html
# Test fixtures are SOURCE, not artifacts. Without these negations the `*.html`
# rule above silently swallowed 10 files the moment they were written:
# tests/fixtures/boards/pages/*.html (the local fake ATS) and
# tests/fixtures/hostile/forms/*.html (the attack corpus). They passed locally
# and would have been absent from the clone CI checks out — a suite that is
# green on one machine and missing its inputs on every other.
# tests/hooks/repo-hygiene.test.mjs fails the build if this ever regresses.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.html
!tests/fixtures/**/*.pdf

# Unattended cycle logs (src/auto/cycle.cmd, via the scripts/auto shim while the Scheduled Task points there) — machine-local run records.
logs/
